    "state": "clear",
    "summary": "Reviewed the full diff for PR #325, which separates local receipt identity requirements from Azure evidence receipts. The core change in bin/fm-crosscheck.py conditionally extends receipt_markers with execution_home and executing_account_home only when evidence_executor is None (local reviews), so Azure credentialless tool VM receipts bind only their distinctive marker and exact base/head SHAs. This is correct: a credentialless Azure VM echoing the model compartment's private paths would prove only a copied literal, not actual identity binding. The new test test_remote_receipt_does_not_impersonate_model_environment verifies the Azure receipt contains list excludes model-only paths, and the Azure prompt test assertions confirm the updated prompt text. Documentation in crosscheck.md and configuration.md is consistent with the implementation. No blocking issues, high-severity concerns, or reproducible defects found.",
